=== layout: section

# Now Expand to Three Genes

=== layout: one-panel

# A New Three-Gene Cross

@body

- *New cross:* a++ / +bc.
- Each ascus contains all four haploid products of one meiosis.
- Find all three pairwise distances and determine gene order.
- Lowercase letters mark mutant alleles; + means wild type.

=== layout: one-panel

# The Six Tetrad Sets

@body

![three gene asci](assets/lect09c-tetrad_worked_examples_bpw/three_gene_asci.svg)

@citation

Given cross: a++ / +bc. Counts describe complete tetrads. Spore positions carry no meiotic-order information.

=== layout: one-panel

# One Pair at a Time

@body

- The cross is a++ / +bc; this gives the parental combinations.
- Each set still contains four spores from one meiosis.
- Cover the unused gene; compare one pair at a time.
- [*Set 6 (702 tetrads)*]{color=#935D00} contains only the original parents: a++ and +bc.
- Set 6 stays [*PD*]{color=#935D00} for every pair. Other sets can change class.
- Keep the set order and all tetrad counts unchanged.

=== include: unordered_tetrad_steps.djot

=== layout: subsection

# Compare A and B

=== layout: one-panel

# A to B: Classify Each Set

@body

![AB homework table with C covered and Set 6 outlined](assets/lect09c-tetrad_worked_examples_bpw/three_gene_homework_ab_question.svg)

For A-B, what class is Set 4?

@citation

Given parents: a++ / +bc. C is covered; read A and B. Gold outline: Set 6 is PD for every pair.

@notes

[*Step 2: Pick A and B*]{color=#B74300}

- Read A and B; C is covered. Set 6 matches the original parents for every pair.
- Parental combinations for this pair: a+ / +b.
- Classify every set using all four spores.
- What class is Set 4?

=== layout: one-panel

# Match the Pair, Not the Count

@body

![AB homework table with C covered and Set 6 outlined](assets/lect09c-tetrad_worked_examples_bpw/three_gene_homework_ab_answer.svg)

[*Set 4 is PD for A-B:*]{color=#935D00} +b and a+ match the parents. Match the pair, not the count.

@citation

Given parents: a++ / +bc. C is covered; read A and B. Gold outline: Set 6 is PD for every pair.

@notes

- Set 4: +b and a+ match the parents. It is [PD]{color=#935D00} for A-B; read only A and B.
- Classify allele combinations, not counts.

=== layout: one-plus-two-panels

# A to B: Add the Class Counts

@left

{table-style=working}
| Set | Tetrads | AB Class |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | 2 | [*NPD*]{color=#007A00 background-color=#BFE6C0} |
| 2 | 5 | [*NPD*]{color=#007A00 background-color=#BFE6C0} |
| 3 | 198 | [*TT*]{color=#A719DB background-color=#E8CCE6} |
| 4 | 11 | [*PD*]{color=#935D00 background-color=#FFE3A3} |
| 5 | 282 | [*PD*]{color=#935D00 background-color=#FFE3A3} |
| [*6*]{color=#935D00 background-color=#FFE3A3} | [*702*]{color=#935D00 background-color=#FFE3A3} | [*PD*]{color=#935D00 background-color=#FFE3A3} |
| [Total]{background-color=#BDD0E4} | [1,200]{background-color=#BDD0E4} | []{background-color=#BDD0E4} |

Read the A-B classifications from the homework table.

@top-right

[*Step 3: Test Linkage*]{color=#6C6C00}

- Add all [PD]{color=#935D00} counts.
- Add all [NPD]{color=#007A00} counts.
- Add all [TT]{color=#A719DB} counts.
- Are the genes linked?

@bottom-right

{table-group="three-gene-results"}
| Pair | Distance (cM) |
| --- | --- |
| [*AB*]{color=#D40000} | [*?*]{color=#D40000} |
| [*AC*]{color=#003FFF} | [*?*]{color=#003FFF} |
| [*BC*]{color=#A719DB} | [*?*]{color=#A719DB} |

@citation

The table summarizes the classifications just completed. Count tetrads, not individual spores.

=== layout: one-plus-two-panels

# A and B Are Linked

@left

{table-style=working}
| Class | Tetrads |
| --- | --- |
| [*PD*]{color=#935D00 background-color=#FFE3A3} | 995 |
| [*NPD*]{color=#007A00 background-color=#BFE6C0} | 7 |
| [*TT*]{color=#A719DB background-color=#E8CCE6} | 198 |
| [Total]{background-color=#BDD0E4} | [1,200]{background-color=#BDD0E4} |

Read the A-B classifications from the homework table.

[PD]{color=#935D00} is much greater than [NPD]{color=#007A00}: *linked*.

@top-right

[*Step 3: Test Linkage*]{color=#6C6C00}

[PD]{color=#935D00} = 11 + 282 + [*702*]{color=#935D00} = 995.

[NPD]{color=#007A00} = 2 + 5 = 7.

[TT]{color=#A719DB} = 198 = 198.


@bottom-right

{table-group="three-gene-results"}
| Pair | Distance (cM) |
| --- | --- |
| [*AB*]{color=#D40000} | [*?*]{color=#D40000} |
| [*AC*]{color=#003FFF} | [*?*]{color=#003FFF} |
| [*BC*]{color=#A719DB} | [*?*]{color=#A719DB} |

@citation

The table summarizes the classifications just completed. Count tetrads, not individual spores.

=== layout: one-plus-two-panels

# A to B: Substitute the Counts

@left

{table-style=working}
| Class | Tetrads |
| --- | --- |
| [*PD*]{color=#935D00 background-color=#FFE3A3} | 995 |
| [*NPD*]{color=#007A00 background-color=#BFE6C0} | 7 |
| [*TT*]{color=#A719DB background-color=#E8CCE6} | 198 |
| [Total]{background-color=#BDD0E4} | [1,200]{background-color=#BDD0E4} |

Read the A-B classifications from the homework table.

@top-right

[*Step 4: Calculate Distance*]{color=#007A00}

$$
D = \frac{\frac{1}{2}(\textcolor{#A719DB}{198}) + 3(\textcolor{#007A00}{7})}{1200} \times 100 \;\mathrm{cM}
$$

Use class counts, not the number of sets.

@bottom-right

